{"finding_id": "FND-001-INF-TOUCH-FRICTION", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "infotainment", "finding_kind": "bmw_weakness", "title": "Touch-first controls for frequent functions pull the driver's eyes off the road", "summary": "Independent testers report that controls around the iDrive controller sit flush in piano-black trim and cannot be found by touch, that airflow sliders below the display are unlit, and that drivers must therefore look away from the road to operate them. This is a usability and attention cost on exactly the functions used most often while driving.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-011d2bed6598", "EXT-11bdeebf3330", "EXT-1a320b96f821", "EXT-1d1bce00cf9f", "EXT-25700d94a471", "EXT-2a2c5b5dd829", "EXT-3b175b0d3e0e", "EXT-44792f5d3af3", "EXT-495ab1143fcc", "EXT-9098f7f898d1", "EXT-aa010bbc1332", "EXT-c92d02395106", "EXT-ee677f7da020", "EXT-f02b234d2b54"], "source_count": 14, "independent_source_count": 6, "average_source_quality": 89.3, "confidence": "high", "stance_summary": {"rows": 14, "by_source_family": {"independent_test_org": 6, "official_manufacturer": 4, "professional_review": 4}, "numeric_rows": 1}, "brands_covered": ["Audi", "BMW", "Tesla"], "vehicles_covered": ["Audi A6 e-tron Avant", "BMW 5er", "BMW 7 / BMW i7", "Tesla vehicle", "compatible vehicles", "i5"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "US", "unknown"], "contradicts": ["FND-003-INF-DISPLAY-STRENGTH"], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-002-INF-SHORTCUTS-LOST", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "infotainment", "finding_kind": "bmw_weakness", "title": "Freely assignable favourite buttons were removed and are missed", "summary": "Independent review notes the previously practical, freely assignable favourite buttons have been removed in favour of programmable on-screen equivalents. Shortcut access to frequently used functions is a regression against the outgoing generation.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-2a2c5b5dd829", "EXT-591a63a622ca", "EXT-669049da2a98", "EXT-8f40f5713e5e", "EXT-a4eca118a68b", "EXT-c92d02395106"], "source_count": 6, "independent_source_count": 6, "average_source_quality": 78.3, "confidence": "medium", "stance_summary": {"rows": 6, "by_source_family": {"independent_test_org": 2, "official_manufacturer": 1, "other": 1, "professional_review": 1, "youtube_review": 1}, "numeric_rows": 0}, "brands_covered": ["BMW", "Tesla"], "vehicles_covered": ["BMW 5er", "Model S and Model X", "i5", "i5 eDrive40"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "unknown"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-003-INF-DISPLAY-STRENGTH", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "infotainment", "finding_kind": "bmw_strength", "title": "The curved display and interaction surfaces read as premium and modern", "summary": "The curved display pairing a 12.3-inch cluster with a 14.9-inch control screen, the Interaction Bar and ambient treatments are described as visually striking and immersive. The screen hardware itself is an asset; the friction sits in the control layer around it.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-2c132f0063a5", "EXT-2d86975d3550", "EXT-32ce31ea00a8", "EXT-3724b0dac16d", "EXT-4612e5201e85", "EXT-52b3d8e0de58", "EXT-6637daf8671f", "EXT-669049da2a98", "EXT-708a38364053", "EXT-92fc9417d169"], "source_count": 10, "independent_source_count": 6, "average_source_quality": 88.5, "confidence": "high", "stance_summary": {"rows": 10, "by_source_family": {"official_manufacturer": 7, "professional_review": 2, "independent_test_org": 1}, "numeric_rows": 0}, "brands_covered": ["Audi", "BMW", "Porsche", "Tesla"], "vehicles_covered": ["Audi A6 e-tron Avant", "BMW i5", "Model S and Model X", "Taycan", "compatible vehicles", "i5"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "US", "unknown"], "contradicts": ["FND-001-INF-TOUCH-FRICTION"], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-004-INF-OTA-COMPETITORS", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "infotainment", "finding_kind": "competitor_strength", "title": "Competitors position infotainment compute and over-the-air upgradeability as a feature", "summary": "Porsche markets a PCM generation with several times the previous computing power and fully over-the-air infotainment updates; Tesla sells an explicit infotainment compute upgrade to older cars. Both frame the head unit as something that improves after delivery, which sets an expectation the 5 Series successor will be measured against.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-03f315426882", "EXT-115e2bf0e978", "EXT-176f015e5785", "EXT-17e030374ef3", "EXT-1a6861bc2602", "EXT-254932c6f911", "EXT-42183ad91e16", "EXT-6ef3c6362f76", "EXT-b461f4e464e4", "EXT-feba1d287bb6"], "source_count": 10, "independent_source_count": 5, "average_source_quality": 83.0, "confidence": "high", "stance_summary": {"rows": 10, "by_source_family": {"official_manufacturer": 7, "customer_forum": 2, "professional_review": 1}, "numeric_rows": 0}, "brands_covered": ["BMW", "Porsche", "Tesla"], "vehicles_covered": ["BMW 7 / BMW i7", "Taycan", "Vehicle", "compatible vehicles", "i5 eDrive 40", "unknown"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "US", "unknown"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-005-INF-SERVICE-PAYWALLS", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "infotainment", "finding_kind": "customer_friction", "title": "Connected services lapse into paid tiers and some conveniences are cost options", "summary": "Connected Drive services are included for an initial period and charged for afterwards, and wireless smartphone charging is available only as a paid option. Digital convenience that arrives time-limited or priced separately is a recurring source of owner irritation.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-06517a904c13", "EXT-666bd4135408", "EXT-a38f2158e985", "EXT-b291d73aafb6"], "source_count": 4, "independent_source_count": 2, "average_source_quality": 93.8, "confidence": "medium", "stance_summary": {"rows": 4, "by_source_family": {"independent_test_org": 3, "official_manufacturer": 1}, "numeric_rows": 1}, "brands_covered": ["BMW"], "vehicles_covered": ["BMW 5er", "BMW 5er (general)", "BMW i5"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "US"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-006-CHG-PEAK-COMPETITIVE", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "charging", "finding_kind": "bmw_strength", "title": "Peak DC charging power of roughly 207-208 kW is measured and competitive", "summary": "Independent testing measured a maximum charging power of 207 kW and 208.4 kW at a CCS fast charger. Peak capability is not the weakness in this car.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-01bc09ebf2a4", "EXT-043ba4285bd3", "EXT-0aa82feb04ff", "EXT-1c1ee3b0b7ce", "EXT-1d5945fa69dc", "EXT-2029be025ac6", "EXT-39006faf46da", "EXT-7ad2eca3a501", "EXT-9f19cf9a6f3d", "EXT-b57fe929d357"], "source_count": 10, "independent_source_count": 6, "average_source_quality": 88.5, "confidence": "high", "stance_summary": {"rows": 10, "by_source_family": {"independent_test_org": 5, "professional_review": 4, "official_manufacturer": 1}, "numeric_rows": 10}, "brands_covered": ["BMW", "Porsche", "Tesla", "other"], "vehicles_covered": ["BMW i5", "Model S", "Taycan Turbo GT", "competitors", "i5", "i5 Touring eDrive40"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "US", "unknown"], "contradicts": ["FND-007-CHG-TAPER"], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-007-CHG-TAPER", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "charging", "finding_kind": "bmw_weakness", "title": "Charging power tapers early, so the session average is far below the peak", "summary": "Independent testers record that the high charging power falls quickly, that power is down to about 42 kW by 80 percent state of charge, that the session average was 135.7 kW, and that the optimum charging window is roughly 1-46 percent. The headline peak overstates what a long-distance stop actually delivers.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-11769dd979b9", "EXT-1c1ee3b0b7ce", "EXT-2029be025ac6", "EXT-39006faf46da", "EXT-5a7ba82bc980", "EXT-5a9ed7e8d69e", "EXT-6d16f75ad45b", "EXT-7f0607630193", "EXT-985cee0d327c", "EXT-a1682ceb6f1a", "EXT-b383113a7e0f", "EXT-b96505959e96"], "source_count": 12, "independent_source_count": 7, "average_source_quality": 82.5, "confidence": "high", "stance_summary": {"rows": 12, "by_source_family": {"professional_review": 10, "independent_test_org": 2}, "numeric_rows": 10}, "brands_covered": ["Audi", "BMW", "Porsche", "Tesla", "unknown"], "vehicles_covered": ["Audi A6 e-tron Avant", "Model S", "Taycan Turbo GT", "i5", "i5 Touring eDrive40", "i5 eDrive40", "unknown"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "unknown"], "contradicts": ["FND-006-CHG-PEAK-COMPETITIVE"], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-008-CHG-TRIP-CADENCE", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "charging", "finding_kind": "bmw_strength", "title": "A 10-80 percent stop of about 30 minutes adds roughly 184 km in 20 minutes", "summary": "Independent measurement puts 10-80 percent at about half an hour, with 184 km of range recovered in a 20-minute stop. Expressed as range-per-stop rather than kilowatts, the long-distance cadence is usable.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-4ab0804b22a6", "EXT-5a645778efeb", "EXT-7f6a75183ca6", "EXT-841ee8835da9", "EXT-861b66b47c47", "EXT-a934e7a45402", "EXT-a93f5a87fa47", "EXT-ac3f2f1bfb03", "EXT-c63e359ee82d", "EXT-cb7d8d479baa"], "source_count": 10, "independent_source_count": 6, "average_source_quality": 83.5, "confidence": "high", "stance_summary": {"rows": 10, "by_source_family": {"professional_review": 6, "independent_test_org": 3, "youtube_review": 1}, "numeric_rows": 8}, "brands_covered": ["BMW", "Chevy", "Genesis", "Porsche", "Tesla"], "vehicles_covered": ["Chevy Silverado EV", "Electrified GV70", "Model S", "Taycan Turbo GT", "i5", "i5 Touring eDrive40", "i5 eDrive40"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "EU", "US", "unknown"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-009-CHG-LOSSES", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "charging", "finding_kind": "bmw_weakness", "title": "Independent testers judge charging losses to be improvable", "summary": "ADAC engineers call the drivetrain efficient but say charging losses could be lower, and note that measured consumption includes DC charging losses. Energy that never reaches the battery is cost and time the customer pays for twice.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-6a65c676dafe", "EXT-b7fceb33e0f9", "EXT-de8857e4a184", "EXT-e8302452d410"], "source_count": 4, "independent_source_count": 2, "average_source_quality": 68.8, "confidence": "low", "stance_summary": {"rows": 4, "by_source_family": {"customer_forum": 3, "independent_test_org": 1}, "numeric_rows": 3}, "brands_covered": ["BMW"], "vehicles_covered": ["i5", "i5 (author measurements)"], "markets_covered": ["DE"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-010-CHG-NETWORK-INTEGRATION", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "charging", "finding_kind": "bmw_strength", "title": "Network breadth and single-app access are an explicit positioning strength", "summary": "BMW states the My BMW App integrates all BMW Charging network providers into one of the largest public charging networks, with access to more than 180,000 points and preferential pricing at IONNA. Note this finding rests mainly on manufacturer sources, so its independence is lower than the measured charging findings.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-179d45be8b40", "EXT-1a3bf0f32852", "EXT-32c363e40cd9", "EXT-423c92c6b95a", "EXT-8aad517ccdfa", "EXT-ad57f8133f44", "EXT-c399fe5f7ef2", "EXT-dd8bcebaa914"], "source_count": 8, "independent_source_count": 5, "average_source_quality": 76.2, "confidence": "medium", "stance_summary": {"rows": 8, "by_source_family": {"official_manufacturer": 5, "other": 2, "professional_review": 1}, "numeric_rows": 0}, "brands_covered": ["BMW", "Tesla"], "vehicles_covered": ["BMW i5", "Model S", "Vehicle", "i5"], "markets_covered": ["US", "unknown"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "Manufacturer-weighted; treat as positioning claim rather than verified performance.", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-011-RNG-REAL-VS-CATALOGUE", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "range", "finding_kind": "customer_friction", "title": "Measured consumption runs far above catalogue figures", "summary": "On the independent test route the 530e consumed 27.1 kWh/100 km in pure electric mode against a combined catalogue figure of 14.7 kWh/100 km. A gap of that size between brochure and road is the mechanism behind range disappointment.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-0a01f9a1b52c", "EXT-0a33ffad3d9a", "EXT-1ff5908e07cd", "EXT-552f0c0ea176", "EXT-9cb807129bca", "EXT-a30c049bc3c7", "EXT-a56fa64cc563", "EXT-ad43f39836a7", "EXT-addfe53d80f3", "EXT-d4a4b0197fda", "EXT-eb34772dd678", "EXT-f2b6da4853dd"], "source_count": 12, "independent_source_count": 4, "average_source_quality": 81.2, "confidence": "high", "stance_summary": {"rows": 12, "by_source_family": {"professional_review": 6, "independent_test_org": 3, "youtube_review": 3}, "numeric_rows": 12}, "brands_covered": ["BMW", "Porsche", "Tesla"], "vehicles_covered": ["BMW 530e Touring M Sportpaket Steptronic", "BMW 5er", "Model S", "Porsche Taycan Turbo GT", "Taycan Turbo GT", "i5 E drive40", "i5 eDrive40"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "ES", "US", "unknown"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-012-RNG-TOURING-PENALTY", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "range", "finding_kind": "market_trend", "title": "The Touring body carries a small measurable efficiency penalty", "summary": "An owner report puts the G61 Touring about 3.2 percent higher in consumption than the G60 saloon. Single-source and self-reported, so treated as a weak signal worth confirming rather than a settled figure.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-0a01f9a1b52c", "EXT-7e531f217341", "EXT-7f25fcfef533", "EXT-beaa8e8ecdfb", "EXT-d1b6f2fa1b66"], "source_count": 5, "independent_source_count": 2, "average_source_quality": 81.0, "confidence": "medium", "stance_summary": {"rows": 5, "by_source_family": {"independent_test_org": 3, "customer_forum": 2}, "numeric_rows": 5}, "brands_covered": ["BMW"], "vehicles_covered": ["BMW 530e Touring M Sportpaket Steptronic", "BMW 550e Touring M Sportpaket xDrive Steptronic", "G60 Limousine (my config)", "G61 Touring vs. G60 Limousine"], "markets_covered": ["DE"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "Low confidence by design: owner-reported, single independence group.", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-013-CMF-SPACE-STRENGTH", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "comfort", "finding_kind": "bmw_strength", "title": "Interior space is a measured, durable strength", "summary": "Independent measurement records 5.06 m overall length, about 10 cm longer than the predecessor, legroom sufficient for nearly 2 m occupants, headroom for nearly 2.10 m, and a 465-litre boot. Space and comfort have been a recognised strength across generations.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-09ee60a49ac0", "EXT-0d634c40ee45", "EXT-0e0e07c08dfd", "EXT-1074c73b5190", "EXT-1c5f66e8dbfb", "EXT-1c8573468625", "EXT-1f258aea3b55", "EXT-2636bf547d8d", "EXT-2b88b102493d", "EXT-5e859b64e6d4", "EXT-c2bac87b2b28", "EXT-dfcef985c310"], "source_count": 12, "independent_source_count": 5, "average_source_quality": 89.2, "confidence": "high", "stance_summary": {"rows": 12, "by_source_family": {"independent_test_org": 6, "professional_review": 4, "official_manufacturer": 2}, "numeric_rows": 6}, "brands_covered": ["BMW"], "vehicles_covered": ["BMW 5er", "BMW i5", "i5 eDrive 40"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "US"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-014-CMF-SUSPENSION-OPTION", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "comfort", "finding_kind": "customer_friction", "title": "Comfortable ride depends on an expensive adaptive suspension option", "summary": "Independent review finds the Sport-package car's suspension very firm and unsuited to comfortable family use, and that ride only smooths out noticeably with the costly Adaptive Suspension Professional option, which is standard only higher in the range. Baseline comfort is therefore configuration-dependent.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-36016a21cc2b", "EXT-4a5441deff24", "EXT-6fa2144e4318", "EXT-7025a44092cf", "EXT-7b78bd1a9eb9", "EXT-7ecbc4c523dc", "EXT-9fe1ebdb7f95", "EXT-a7b295148edc", "EXT-ad4c0bf445a7", "EXT-bebc89b9bd8a", "EXT-cd33b1c17990", "EXT-da000e6d3edb"], "source_count": 12, "independent_source_count": 5, "average_source_quality": 87.5, "confidence": "high", "stance_summary": {"rows": 12, "by_source_family": {"independent_test_org": 6, "professional_review": 6}, "numeric_rows": 1}, "brands_covered": ["BMW"], "vehicles_covered": ["BMW 530e", "BMW 5er", "BMW i5", "BMW i5 M60 xDrive", "BMW i5 eDrive40", "i5 M60", "i5 eDrive 40", "iX xDrive50"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "unknown"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-015-CMF-QUIET-CABIN", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "comfort", "finding_kind": "bmw_strength", "title": "Cabin noise is measured at roughly 64.7-65.0 dB(A) at 130 km/h", "summary": "Independent measurement puts interior noise at 130 km/h between 64.7 and 65.0 dB(A) across variants, with professional reviews describing the cabin as very quiet to about 160 km/h. Refinement at autobahn speed is an evidenced strength.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-00edeb514d5d", "EXT-439ffac97a8f", "EXT-58f4d9d500ab", "EXT-6b85726bc4d0", "EXT-6e33c5063046", "EXT-7f89db6c4bfb", "EXT-87b211dd4572", "EXT-a21eeef23ee7", "EXT-bced0e459d23", "EXT-ce2615e71734"], "source_count": 10, "independent_source_count": 7, "average_source_quality": 82.5, "confidence": "high", "stance_summary": {"rows": 10, "by_source_family": {"professional_review": 5, "independent_test_org": 3, "youtube_review": 2}, "numeric_rows": 7}, "brands_covered": ["Audi", "BMW", "Mercedes Benz", "Tesla"], "vehicles_covered": ["Audi A6 e-tron Avant", "BMW 530e Touring M Sportpaket Steptronic", "BMW 550e Touring M Sportpaket xDrive Steptronic", "BMW i5 eDrive40", "EQE500 SUV", "I5", "Model S", "i5 eDrive 40"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "unknown"], "contradicts": [], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
{"finding_id": "FND-016-CMF-DETAIL-QUALITY", "schema_version": "1", "topic": "comfort", "finding_kind": "bmw_weakness", "title": "Specific interior details undermine the premium impression", "summary": "Independent review states that a set of interior details feel not very premium-like and tarnish the perception of quality, with piano-black surfaces and cheap-feeling touch buttons in the door called out. This sits alongside a generally good workmanship score, and both observations are preserved.", "evidence_ids": ["EXT-3a7c762b1299", "EXT-49a9593031a9", "EXT-5150db5e043b", "EXT-6580beb1adba", "EXT-670390fc7e54", "EXT-84293e98e6fe", "EXT-bcc18bf21c48", "EXT-d398f9d1828a", "EXT-f4fdd28adc13"], "source_count": 9, "independent_source_count": 5, "average_source_quality": 77.2, "confidence": "medium", "stance_summary": {"rows": 9, "by_source_family": {"independent_test_org": 3, "youtube_review": 3, "customer_forum": 2, "professional_review": 1}, "numeric_rows": 0}, "brands_covered": ["Audi", "BMW"], "vehicles_covered": ["A6 Avant e-tron performance (2025)", "BMW 5er", "I5", "i5 (5er)", "i5 Touring (G61)", "i5 eDrive40"], "markets_covered": ["DE", "ES", "unknown"], "contradicts": ["FND-013-CMF-SPACE-STRENGTH"], "notes": "", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:18:37Z"}
